<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Wadhwan State</h1><p class="st-meta">1630 CE – 1948 CE (approx.) · capital Wadhwan</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Jhala Rajput state of Kathiawar on the Bhogavo river, one of the branches of the Halvad ruling house.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Wadhwan was founded in 1630 by a cadet of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jhala">Jhala</a> house of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/halvad">Halvad</a>, the line of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/dhrangadhra-state">Dhrangadhra State</a>. The town had an older history as a medieval fortified centre.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Thakore Sahibs ruled a territory of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a> villages, paying tribute to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaekwads">Gaekwads</a> before British protection after 1807. A British civil station grew up beside the town, later Surendranagar, and the railway made the area a cotton market. It was a nine-gun salute state.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Wadhwan merged into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/saurashtra-state">United State of Saurashtra</a> in 1948 and became part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a> in 1960. Its old town is now part of Surendranagar.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/wadhwan-state.jpg" alt="Wadhwan State" width="320" height="214"><figcaption>Image: McSush · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wadhwan_flag.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1630 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Wadhwan</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gujarati</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Wadhwan</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1789&amp;focus=wadhwan-state" aria-label="Wadhwan State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6592 1350 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Wadhwan State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6912 1606L7364 1601M6912 1606L7364 1602M6912 1606L6896 1610"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7364 1601h0M7364 1602h0M6896 1610h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6912 1606h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6912 1606h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1789&amp;focus=wadhwan-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
